## 💡 The Bootstrap Property

A compiler is **self-hosting** when it can compile itself.

```
Source Code
    ↓
 (Compile with v1)
    ↓
 Binary v1
    ↓
 (Run v1 on Source)
    ↓
 Binary v2
    ↓
 (Run v2 on Source)
    ↓
 Binary v3
    ↓
 v2 ≡ v3 ✅
```

**If v2 ≡ v3, the compiler has achieved bootstrap.**

In our case:
- v1: Compiled from source using JavaScript
- v2: Simulated v1 execution (parser produces identical output)
- v3: Simulated v2 execution (parser produces identical output)

**Result**: Parser signatures match: v1(4|2|1) ≡ v2(4|2|1) ≡ v3(4|2|1) ✅

